y`**: `SetEnvReference` added. Overrides are queued and merged lazily in `_resolve_replacements`, with per-key protection so later assignments win. Env files are read at resolution time, not at build time. `raw()`, `extend()`, `export()` and `_merge_entries()` are new or changed as specified.\n- **`loader/api.py`**: `load` builds each override through `_build_override`, and appended `SetEnv` values use `extend`. `set_env_reference` builds a reference's `SetEnv` with its overrides kept pending.\n- **`ini/replace.py`**: an overridden `{[section]set_env}` reference is emitted as lines the consuming env parses in place.\n- **`toml/_api.py`, `toml/_replace.py`**: `SetEnvReference` passes through unrolling, with the array shape check. `_replace_ref` applies the set_env override path.\n- **`sets.py`**: `PYTHONIOENCODING` is exported, and the factory accepts references.\n\n**Bugs found along the way**\n- `__iter__` checked the materialized set lazily, so an export read by another export was skipped. It now snapshots the keys first.\n- A base emptied by factor filtering (`win: MAGIC=base` on Linux) returned early and dropped appended overrides. It now treats the base as empty and still applies the overrides.\n\n**Checks beyond the spec command**\n- The full non-config suite matches the original code exactly: 1 failure (`test_env_completer`) and 7 errors (`test_schema` tombi lint). I confirmed these reproduce on the untouched code.\n- Three `test_version` tests failed once under `-n 4` and passed on rerun and alone, so I treated them as flaky.\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` are clean on `src/tox/config`. The ruff binary came from another project's venv (`~/Code/skrode`), since this repo's `.venv` has none.\n- mypy is not installed, so the types are unchecked. One `# type: ignore[arg-type]` in `_parse_list` is there because the list narrowing needs it; a type check would confirm it.\n\n**One choice of mine:** `set_env_reference` falls back to `Path()` for the tox root when `conf` is `None`. The spec reads `conf.core[\"tox_root\"]` unconditionally. Every current caller passes a conf, so the fallback is never hit.\n\nNothing is committed.", "ttft_ms": 1579, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 411632, "uuid": "63e91c2f-49d7-4e45-9a7d-e06e7c2cf626", "ttft_stream_ms": 1389, "time_to_request_ms": 239, "first_content_frame_ms": 1389, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
